From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: sysconfig: report linux-aarch64_ilp32 on AArch64 ILP32

An AArch64 ILP32 python reported linux-aarch64, and packaging (pip) takes
linux_aarch64 with 32-bit pointers for 32-bit ARM: its tags became
linux_armv8l/armv7l, and with musl also musllinux_*_armv7l/armv8l, so pip
would install AArch32 wheels from PyPI that cannot be loaded. With its own
platform the tags are musllinux_1_x_aarch64_ilp32, linux_aarch64_ilp32
and any.

Only the run-time path changes: cross builds set _PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM,
which is returned before this code.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
--- a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
@@ -659,6 +659,11 @@
                 "x86_64": "x86_64",
             }[machine]
         else:
+            # AArch64 ILP32 (32-bit pointers, AArch64 instructions): its own
+            # platform, so that wheel tags do not take it for 32-bit ARM
+            # (packaging maps linux_aarch64 with 32-bit pointers to armv8l)
+            if machine == "aarch64" and sys.maxsize < 2**32:
+                machine = "aarch64_ilp32"
             # At least on Linux/Intel, 'machine' is the processor --
             # i386, etc.
             # XXX what about Alpha, SPARC, etc?
